---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/ui/Container.astro";
import Button from "@/components/ui/Button.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="What Worm Studio is, and how we work - an SEO, GEO & AEO agency done properly, never automated."
  path="/about"
>
  <Container grid class="pt-20 pb-24">
    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-8">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-ink leading-tight">
        A UK search visibility agency. Real articles, real SEO expertise, zero AI.
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 mt-8">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted">
        Worm Studio exists because search stopped being just Google.
        People now ask AI tools like ChatGPT for recommendations on all things from best products, services and industry experts.
        The honest truth is most businesses aren't sure whether they are being recommended, if they are showing up in search and prompt results, what what to do if they aren't. 
        We help brands and businesses get found in both. With human-written articles and content, properly structured webpages, and absolutely no templated or automated filler.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        SEO, GEO, and AEO aren't three separate services here - they're
        one connected system. The technical work (schema, structure,
        crawlability) and the content work both matter, and neither one
        works well without the other.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        Worm Studio is run by Daniel Glazebrook - a full-stack web
        developer with a design background and over a decade in SEO and digital marketing. 
        The studio is new; the expertise behind it isn't.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <Button href="/daniel-glazebrook" variant="outline">Meet the founder</Button>
        <Button href="/#approach" variant="text">Read our approach</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
